{#-
  Ondo Global Markets — mintWithAttestation / redeemWithAttestation on
  Ondo's GMTokenManager.

  The GMTokenManager is canonical-per-chain, resolved from
  aliases.ondo_gm.router inside the template (NOT a param). GM token
  addresses and payment assets live in aliases.tokens (the standard
  token registry).

  Required template params:
    gm_tokens      — list of GM token alias keys (e.g.
                     ["HYGon", "TLTon", "SHYon", "IEFon"]). Each entry
                     resolved via aliases.tokens[<key>] with no
                     existence guard ⇒ render-time error if missing.
    payment_assets — list of token alias keys allowed as depositToken
                     (mint) and receiveToken (redeem) (e.g. ["USDC"]).
                     Each resolved via aliases.tokens[<key>], same
                     loud-fail behaviour.

  Resolved from aliases (NOT params):
    aliases.ondo_gm.router — GMTokenManager contract
    aliases.tokens[<key>]  — each gm_tokens entry
    aliases.tokens[<key>]  — each payment_assets entry

  Quote (IGMTokenManager.Quote, 9 fields in ABI order):
    0 chainId        — must equal block.chainid
    1 attestationId  — single-use: the GMTokenManager records it in
                       executedAttestationIds, a replay reverts
    2 userId         — must equal the Ondo ID that OndoIDRegistry holds
                       for msg.sender (the Safe); the quote is bound to
                       that Ondo ID, not to an address
    3 asset          — GM token bought or sold; must be registered on
                       the GMTokenManager
    4 price          — USD per GM token, 18 decimals; checked against
                       Ondo's sanity-check oracle
    5 quantity       — GM tokens minted (mint) or pulled and burned
                       (redeem)
    6 expiration     — unix seconds; reverts once block.timestamp >
                       expiration
    7 side           — QuoteSide (uint8): BUY (0) for mint, SELL (1) for
                       redeem, enforced per entry point
    8 additionalData — opaque bytes32
  Ondo signs the Quote off-chain (EIP-712, domain "OndoGMTokenManager"
  version "1"); the GMTokenManager recovers the signer on-chain and
  requires it to hold ATTESTATION_SIGNER_ROLE. Both entry points also
  revert outside Ondo's issuance hours (IssuanceHours.checkIsValidHours).

  Trailing arguments:
    mint   — depositToken, depositTokenAmount. With USDon as depositToken
             the GMTokenManager pulls exactly quantity * price / 1e18 and
             ignores depositTokenAmount. With any other token it pulls
             exactly depositTokenAmount, swaps it to USDon through the
             USDonManager and refunds the USDon surplus to the caller.
    redeem — receiveToken, minimumReceiveAmount. minimumReceiveAmount is
             the USDonManager swap floor, used only when receiveToken is
             not USDon.

  Scoping:
    - quote: only `asset` (index 3) is pinned; the other fields are
      fixed by Ondo's signature. The tuple is wrapped in an `or` of
      per-asset `matches` so the role can mint and redeem any enumerated
      GM token but no others. When gm_tokens has EXACTLY 1 entry, the
      `or` wrapper is dropped and a bare `matches` is emitted — `or` with
      <2 conditions is degenerate and rejected at apply time
      (action/apply/toSdkTargets.ts, "'or' requires ≥ 2 conditions").
    - signature is left as `dynamic` `pass`; the GMTokenManager verifies
      it on-chain.
    - depositToken / receiveToken are pinned to `oneOf(payment_assets)`
      (`equal_to` is semantically equivalent for length 1; we keep oneOf
      for uniformity).
    - depositTokenAmount / minimumReceiveAmount are left `pass`.
-#}
{%- from "_macros/common.tmpl" import approve -%}
{%- set router = aliases.ondo_gm.router -%}
roles:
{%- for asset in payment_assets %}
  {{ approve(aliases.tokens[asset], router) | indent(2) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for key in gm_tokens %}
  {{ approve(aliases.tokens[key], router) | indent(2) }}
{%- endfor %}

  - address: "{{ router }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function mintWithAttestation((uint256 chainId, uint256 attestationId, bytes32 userId, address asset, uint256 price, uint256 quantity, uint256 expiration, uint8 side, bytes32 additionalData) quote, bytes signature, address depositToken, uint256 depositTokenAmount)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: quote
            param_type: "tuple"
{%- if gm_tokens | length == 1 %}
            operator: "matches"
            conditions:
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "equal_to"
                value: "{{ aliases.tokens[gm_tokens[0]] }}"
                value_type: "address"
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "pass"
{%- else %}
            operator: "or"
            conditions:
              {%- for key in gm_tokens %}
              - operator: "matches"
                conditions:
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "equal_to"
                    value: "{{ aliases.tokens[key] }}"
                    value_type: "address"
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "pass"
              {%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
          - name: signature
            param_type: "dynamic"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: depositToken
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "oneOf"
            values:
              {%- for asset in payment_assets %}
              - "{{ aliases.tokens[asset] }}"
              {%- endfor %}
            value_type: "address"
          - name: depositTokenAmount
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"

      - signature: "function redeemWithAttestation((uint256 chainId, uint256 attestationId, bytes32 userId, address asset, uint256 price, uint256 quantity, uint256 expiration, uint8 side, bytes32 additionalData) quote, bytes signature, address receiveToken, uint256 minimumReceiveAmount)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: quote
            param_type: "tuple"
{%- if gm_tokens | length == 1 %}
            operator: "matches"
            conditions:
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "equal_to"
                value: "{{ aliases.tokens[gm_tokens[0]] }}"
                value_type: "address"
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "pass"
              - operator: "pass"
{%- else %}
            operator: "or"
            conditions:
              {%- for key in gm_tokens %}
              - operator: "matches"
                conditions:
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "equal_to"
                    value: "{{ aliases.tokens[key] }}"
                    value_type: "address"
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "pass"
                  - operator: "pass"
              {%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
          - name: signature
            param_type: "dynamic"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: receiveToken
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "oneOf"
            values:
              {%- for asset in payment_assets %}
              - "{{ aliases.tokens[asset] }}"
              {%- endfor %}
            value_type: "address"
          - name: minimumReceiveAmount
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
